#+TITLE: EPURE profile starts application before the target document guard
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation
#+BRANCH: codex/alfe-com-job-drawing

* Evidence
Pascal confirms that SCHME !339 job565287 on runner0 is blocked on the SCHME
news dialogue (with mojibake), before READY, not the foreign-DWG warning.
The shared RFR guard is loaded before EPURE's explicit control script, but
the epure plugin previously activated its profile in :after-app, before the
requested DWG was opened. A guard loaded later cannot prevent earlier native
profile/document initialization. This does not prove an early NOP restoration.

* Correction under qualification
Add :after-document to both Windows COM emitters; activate EPURE's profile
there, before runtime trust setup and control. The RFR caller installs its
factorized guard in that exact document first, requires a native ACK and
restores its temporary trusted paths. A missing ACK, wrong document or wrong
explicit profile fails startup; no business assertion is simulated.
